        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Show Your Tin Cup Spirit – Run. Give. Celebrate.</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/tin-cup-2026-race-start.webp" alt="Show Your Tin Cup Spirit – Run. Give. Celebrate." loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>The Community Foundation of Teton Valley invites the valley to gather at Driggs City Park on Saturday, July 18, for the 19th Annual Tin Cup Challenge. One of Teton Valley&rsquo;s largest annual celebrations of giving, the event brings together more than 60 nonprofits and has raised over $30.8 million during the past 18 years to strengthen organizations serving every corner of Teton Valley.</p>

<p>Hosted by the Community Foundation of Teton Valley, the Tin Cup Challenge reflects the Foundation&rsquo;s mission to connect people, resources, and nonprofits to strengthen our entire community. Unlike traditional fundraisers that benefit a single organization, Tin Cup gifts support many nonprofits and are partially matched by Business and Community Challengers, multiplying your impact.</p>

<p><strong>Whether you run, volunteer, cheer, or give, everyone is welcome and makes an impact!</strong></p>

<h3><strong>Run (or Walk) for Good</strong></h3>

<ul>
<li><strong>9:00 AM</strong> – Timed 5K/10K races</li>
<li><strong>9:03 AM</strong> – Family-friendly Fun Run/Walk <em>(Free with early registration)</em>
<ul>
<li>Sign up early at <a href="https://www.tincupchallenge.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">www.TinCupChallenge.com</a></li>
<li><strong>Day-of registrations increase by $10</strong> for both the Fun Run/Walk and competitive races. Cash-only registrations on Event Day.</li>
<li>All racers get a <strong>free Tin Cup T-shirt</strong> <em>(while supplies last)</em>.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>

<h3><strong>Stay for the Fun</strong></h3>

<p>After the run, enjoy:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Free community breakfast</strong></li>
<li>Booths from <strong>over 60 nonprofits</strong></li>
<li><strong>Diaper Derby</strong>, <strong>soap hockey</strong>, <strong>folkloric dancing</strong>, and a <strong>flight simulator</strong>!</li>
<li>A petting zoo with horses, mini-horses, adoptable puppies, and more!</li>
</ul>

<h3><strong>Dress to Impress</strong></h3>

<p>Support your favorite nonprofit with spirited costumes. Your organization could win the <strong>Tin Cup Spirit Award</strong>, with prizes of $200, $100, and $75. Awards begin at <strong>10:30 AM</strong> on the Event Stage, including the <strong>Dawn Banks Award</strong>, <strong>Race Awards</strong>, and <strong>Spirit Awards</strong>.</p>

<h3><strong>Multiply Your Impact</strong></h3>

<p>Every dollar matters. Every gift counts. Give today by <strong>cash, check, stocks, or online at</strong> <a href="https://www.tincupchallenge.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">www.TinCupChallenge.com</a>, and your donation will be <strong>partially matched</strong> thanks to <strong>Business &amp; Community Challengers</strong>. <strong>The deadline to give is Friday, July 24, at 5 PM.</strong></p>

<p><strong>Engage with your community, support important causes, and have fun!</strong> You can also visit us at the Community Foundation&rsquo;s Farmers Market booth in <strong>Driggs</strong> on Fridays from 9 AM to 1 PM through July 24.</p>

<p>According to Brian Thysell, program manager, <em>&ldquo;One of the best parts of Event Day is watching people discover nonprofits they may not have known about and meet the people behind them. Whether you&rsquo;re there to race, volunteer, or enjoy breakfast with your neighbors, it&rsquo;s a chance to see how many people are doing good across Teton Valley.&rdquo;</em></p>

<p>For nearly two decades, the Tin Cup Challenge has been a summer tradition celebrating the nonprofits, volunteers, and donors who make Teton Valley an extraordinary place to call home. <strong>Celebrate generosity. Give locally. Accept the Challenge.</strong></p>

<p>Questions? Visit <a href="https://www.cftetonvalley.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">www.cftetonvalley.org</a>, call <strong>208.354.0230</strong>, email <strong><a href="mailto:info@cftetonvalley.org">info@cftetonvalley.org</a></strong>, or stop by our office at 189 N. Main St., Suite 112, Driggs.</p>
